[[include info:start]]
**SCP-L953:** Secure, Contain, __//Protect//__
**Author:** [[*user aismallard]] ([[[aismallard|Author Page]]])

Thanks to [[*user Kufat]] and [[*user Trintavon]] for critique, and in particular the assistance of [[*user Dysadron]].
[[include info:end]]

[[image https://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-l953/thumbnail.webp class="crom-thumbnail" style="display: none"]]

**Item #:** SCP-L953

**Object Class:** Keter

**Special Containment Procedures:** Human interaction with SCP-L953 is strictly limited. Personnel wishing to enter its chamber must submit to a full psychological evaluation and receive approval from the SCP-L953 Containment Committee. Prior to any planned contact with the anomaly, personnel must submit to decontamination and don Class-VIII biohazard suits.

SCP-L953 instances are maintained in a 220,000 m^^3^^ containment chamber at Site-97. This chamber is hermetically sealed, with alternating layers of lead (8 cm) and ceramic (5 cm) to inhibit psychic radiation. A Class-XVII biosphere system has been installed inside the chamber, providing artificial sunlight, precipitation, and air (heavily scrubbed to remove pollutants). --Additional SCP-L953 populations are kept in Bio Area-12 and Site-403.--

The containment chamber is populated with fauna and flora per Document 1037-Kappa. Whenever possible, repopulation of insects, trimming and replanting, and other maintenance tasks are to be performed via remotely-controlled drone.

Should an instance of SCP-L953 escape, the site will enter lockdown and the recontainment team is to carry out Procedure 207-Quogue. All other human personnel must immediately proceed to Insulated Influence Chambers (see Site-97 schematics for further details).

Current research efforts are directed towards:
* Improving psychic filtration in the SCP-L953 containment chamber.
* Understanding and lessening health risks from human/SCP-L953 contact.
* Developing paramedicinal procedure for mental recovery after contact incidents.
* Substantially growing and expanding the SCP-L953 population.

**Description:** SCP-L953 refers to the anomalous species //Locustella vitella//, a type of grasshopper warbler, a small bird with telepathic abilities. The species is highly in-tune with its human-built environment, with instances beginning morning song at exactly 7:00 AM (the most common alarm clock setting on-site), along with a strong correlation between SCP-L953 evening chatter and dinner activity in the Site-97 canteen. Additionally, numerous researchers have shared anecdotes of SCP-L953 instances spontaneously performing the melodies of their favorite songs during testing and observation.

[[collapsible show="▸ Open Attached Image" hide="▾ Close Attached Image"]]
[[include component:image-block
| name=https://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-l953/warbler.webp
| width=280px
| caption=SCP-L953 in captivity.
]]
[[/collapsible]]

SCP-L953 poses no threat to humans. However, for unclear reasons, increasing computerization and adoption of the internet has created a psychic environment that is deeply toxic to SCP-L953. Telepathic shielding and human contact procedures were effective at preserving its population until the mainstream adoption of internet-enabled consumer electronics, which has resulted in a mass die-off.

SCP-L953 is extinct in the wild. At present, there are --34,607-- (1980) --12,120-- (1990) --4,066-- (2000) --817-- (2010) 54 instances (2020) in containment.

**Addendum:** The SCP-L953 Containment Committee has confirmed that the anomaly is now Neutralized. This file is slated to be rewritten.

